  mastery:{facts:[[1, "Structural geology studies deformation in rocks from {outcrop|global|atomic|planetary} to regional scale."], [1, "Tectonics studies plate interactions from {regional to global|outcrop to regional|crystal to outcrop|local to outcrop} scale."], [1, "{Endogenous|Exogenous|Sedimentary|Atmospheric} processes are driven by Earth's internal heat."], [1, "{Exogenous|Endogenous|Magmatic|Tectonic} processes happen at and above the Earth's surface."], [2, "The three drivers of Earth's dynamics are heat, gravity and {rotation|wind|water|magnetism}."], [2, "Radiogenic heat comes from the decay of K, Th and {U|Fe|Ni|Si}."], [2, "{Primordial|Radiogenic|Solar|Geothermal} heat is left over from the formation of the Earth."], [2, "Solar heat mainly controls {exogenous|endogenous|magmatic|metamorphic} processes such as weather, erosion and weathering."], [2, "The {geothermal gradient|Moho|geodynamo|asthenosphere} describes how temperature rises with depth."], [2, "Because of {gravity|rotation|solar heat|wind}, dense materials sink and light (buoyant) materials rise."], [2, "Rotation affects the atmosphere, ocean currents and the {outer core|inner core|crust|mesosphere}."], [3, "The three chemical layers are the crust, the mantle and the {core|lithosphere|asthenosphere|mesosphere}."], [3, "The crust is {5 to 70|500 to 700|1 to 2|100 to 200} km thick."], [3, "The mantle is made of {peridotitic|granitic|basaltic|limestone} (ultramafic) silicate rock."], [3, "The core is made of an {Fe-Ni|Si-O|K-Th|Ca-Mg} alloy."], [3, "The boundary between the crust and the mantle is the {Moho|Gutenberg discontinuity|geodynamo|asthenosphere}."], [3, "The boundary between the mantle and the core is the {Gutenberg|Mohorovičić|Conrad|Wegener} discontinuity."], [3, "The Gutenberg discontinuity lies at about {2900|35|70|6378} km depth."], [3, "The Earth's radius is {6378|637|2900|12756} km."], [3, "The deepest borehole is about {12|70|2|120} km deep and never reached the Moho."], [4, "{Xenoliths|Ophiolites|Meteorites|Geodes} are fragments of deeper rock carried up inside magma."], [4, "{Ophiolites|Xenoliths|Chondrites|Batholiths} are pieces of oceanic crust exposed on land."], [4, "Ophiolites are pushed up onto continental crust by {obduction|subduction|erosion|weathering}."], [4, "{Chondritic|Iron|Martian|Lunar} meteorites formed from the same solar nebula as the Earth, so they have the same composition."], [4, "A classic xenolith is peridotite (dunite) carried up in {basalt|granite|sandstone|limestone}."], [4, "Diamond-bearing {eclogite|granite|sandstone|limestone} is a classic xenolith."], [4, "Laboratory experiments show how rocks behave at high {pressure and temperature|speed and light|humidity and wind|salt and acidity}."], [5, "From the surface down: lithosphere, asthenosphere, {mesosphere|crust|mantle|geosphere}, outer core, inner core."], [5, "The lithosphere is the crust plus the {uppermost mantle|outer core|lower mantle|inner core}."], [5, "The asthenosphere is {plastic|rigid|liquid|gaseous}: a very viscous liquid."], [5, "The {outer core|inner core|mesosphere|asthenosphere} is the only liquid layer."], [5, "The inner core is rigid because of the higher {pressure|temperature|water content|rotation}."], [5, "Tectonic plates move on the {asthenosphere|mesosphere|inner core|outer core}."], [5, "The physical layers reflect {mechanical behaviour|chemical composition|age|colour}: rigid, plastic or liquid."], [5, "The mesosphere is the {lower|upper|whole|uppermost} mantle and is more rigid than the asthenosphere."], [6, "Seismic waves are caused by {earthquakes|tides|winds|the magnetic field}."], [6, "Seismic wave speed depends on the rigidity and {density|colour|age|magnetism} of the material."], [6, "Mapping slow and fast seismic regions in the mantle is called mantle {tomography|topography|stratigraphy|petrology}."], [6, "Electric currents in the moving liquid outer core create the magnetic field: the {geodynamo|geothermal gradient|Moho|asthenosphere}."], [6, "Magnetic poles move ({polar wander|continental drift|subduction|obduction}) and can reverse."], [7, "The core lies between 2900 and {6378|637|1200|12756} km depth."], [7, "The core has a density of about {10 to 13|2.7|3.3 to 5.5|1} g/cm³."], [7, "The mantle has a density of about {3.3 to 5.5|10 to 13|2.7|1} g/cm³."], [7, "The mantle lies between about 30 and {2900|6378|670|35} km depth."], [7, "We only have samples from the {uppermost|lowest|whole|deepest} part of the mantle."], [7, "There are no samples of the core, so it is studied with experiments and {modelling|boreholes|xenoliths|ophiolites}."], [8, "Oceanic crust forms at {mid-ocean ridges|mountain belts|deep trenches|continental rifts} by mantle melting."], [8, "Oceanic crust is {5 to 7|35|70|10 to 13} km thick."], [8, "Oceanic crust has a density of about {3|2.7|5.5|13} g/cm³."], [8, "Oceanic crust is at most about {200|2000|20|4000} million years old."], [8, "Oceanic crust is made of basalt and {gabbro|granite|gneiss|limestone}, plus deep-sea sediments."], [8, "From the sea floor down: sediments, {pillow lavas|gabbro|peridotite|granite}, sheeted dykes, gabbro."], [8, "Continental crust is on average about {35|7|70|200} km thick."], [8, "Continental crust has a density of about {2.7|3|5.5|10} g/cm³, so it is buoyant."], [8, "Continental crust can be up to {billions of|200 million|2000|20 million} years old."], [9, "The five spheres are geosphere, hydrosphere, {cryosphere|lithosphere|asthenosphere|mesosphere}, atmosphere and biosphere."], [9, "Permafrost belongs to the {cryosphere|hydrosphere|atmosphere|geosphere}."], [9, "The {biosphere|geosphere|hydrosphere|atmosphere} is all living organisms and their ecosystems."], [9, "The {hydrosphere|cryosphere|biosphere|geosphere} is all water on, within and above the Earth's surface."]]},
